swa-flex-attention.patch  (notes/hardware-spark.md, proposal P3; claims C12, C115; check SQ72)

Opt-in block-sparse sliding window: model config "swa_impl": "flex" runs SWA through torch's flex_attention with
a sliding-window BlockMask (only the ~3 key blocks a 128-query block can see are computed), instead of SDPA with a
dense [T, T] bool mask (which forces the non-flash kernel and computes all T^2 scores). Default "mask" keeps every
existing config bit-identical. torch 2.14.1 ships an sm_12x flex default (bf16, head_dim 64: 128x64 tiles, 2
stages, 4 warps) that fits the 99 KiB per-block shared-memory limit. Variable-length inference (sample(), T not
a multiple of 128) falls back to the mask path, so generation never recompiles per token.
Apply after SQ72 passes: git apply notes/patches/swa-flex-attention.patch ; then register an E1/E2-style A/B
(one ingredient: SWA kernel) before switching any registered config.

